1
00:00:00,330 --> 00:00:03,330
(Transcribed by TurboScribe. Go Unlimited to remove this message.) Mark Smith needed to get a job.

2
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:05,230
There was one problem.

3
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,670
Mark was a bit lazy.

4
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:10,770
He wanted to do something easy.

5
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:14,690
I know, he said, I can be a

6
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:14,990
waiter.

7
00:00:15,870 --> 00:00:17,890
I don't think that's the best job for

8
00:00:17,890 --> 00:00:19,330
you, said his mom.

9
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:21,970
Why not, Mark replied.

10
00:00:22,550 --> 00:00:24,710
He thought the job looked very simple.

11
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:27,690
All I have to do is clean tables,

12
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:31,170
said Mark, plus I would get big tips.

13
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:34,430
Mark got hired as a waiter in a

14
00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:35,070
small cafe.

15
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,730
He soon realized his mom was right.

16
00:00:39,610 --> 00:00:42,110
Everyone who ate left a big mess on

17
00:00:42,110 --> 00:00:42,630
the table.

18
00:00:43,510 --> 00:00:45,090
Mark hated cleaning up.

19
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:47,690
He was very slow at it, too.

20
00:00:48,510 --> 00:00:50,630
He kept dropping plates on the floor.

21
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:54,550
To top it off, he wasn't very nice

22
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:55,290
to customers.

23
00:00:56,070 --> 00:00:58,010
They left him small tips.

24
00:00:59,030 --> 00:01:01,550
Mark was fired after three days.
